WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.480
This is the Strategya Summary.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.090
The Catalog shows one card per strategy.

3
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.920
The Summary puts all 23 in one table,

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.580
measured on the same window,

5
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.530
and ranked.

6
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.530
Let's read it from the top.

7
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.600
First, the badge.

8
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.450
Everything on this page is a simulated backtest,

9
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.950
not real performance.

10
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.560
Next to it, when the last signal was calculated,

11
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.040
and how long ago.

12
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.440
Then, the window.

13
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.880
Every product is measured on the same window,

14
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.040
from May 2023 to today,

15
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.670
and ranked by MAR,

16
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.280
which is CAGR divided by max drawdown.

17
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.760
Because the window is shared,

18
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.300
these figures differ from each product page,

19
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.560
which uses its own.

20
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.050
You can choose the window.

21
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.510
Six months, one year,

22
00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.840
two years, or the common window.

23
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.440
Tap one year, and the whole

24
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.900
table is recomputed and ranked again.

25
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.060
One warning.

26
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.600
On six months, CAGR is annualized,

27
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.140
so it can look extreme.

28
00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.640
Below the windows, the filters.

29
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.680
All, sovereign, rotation, one day,

30
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.340
12 hour, with shorts,

31
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.270
with stocks.

32
00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:05.120
Tap rotation, and only the eight rotation products remain,

33
00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.810
ranked among themselves.

34
00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.160
Now the columns.

35
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.840
Let's use BTC 1D, the flagship from the Catalog video,

36
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.160
as the example.

37
00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:13.890
Product.

38
00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.970
The name, then its time frame,

39
00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.370
its type, and its sleeve.

40
00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.730
Sovereign trades one asset.

41
00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.140
Rotation moves between several.

42
00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.840
Long only, never shorts.

43
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:24.960
Multiplier.

44
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.850
Final capital divided by initial capital.

45
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:34.010
4.54 times means $1000 became $4540 in this backtest.

46
00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.280
CAGR.

47
00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.920
The annualized return.

48
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.930
54% a year.

49
00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.440
It is what makes windows of different length comparable.

50
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.700
Max drawdown.

51
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.860
The deepest fall from a

52
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.370
peak before a new high.

53
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.490
17.5%.

54
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.610
It is what you would

55
00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.320
have had to sit through.

56
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:49.910
MAR.

57
00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:52.880
CAGR divided by max drawdown.

58
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.530
In bold, because it is the

59
00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.210
figure the table ranks by.

60
00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.210
3.12.

61
00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.870
Three points of yearly return

62
00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.710
for every point of drawdown.

63
00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.670
Simply holding the asset usually lands near one.

64
00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:04.290
Sharpe.

65
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.730
Return divided by its volatility.

66
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.640
It penalizes every swing,

67
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.880
up or down.

68
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.370
Above one is good.

69
00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.280
Above two is very good.

70
00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.000
Hold.

71
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.980
The same three figures.

72
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.980
CAGR, drawdown, and MAR.

73
00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:21.770
For buying bitcoin at the start and never selling.

74
00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.830
34, 53, and 0.64.

75
00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.450
This is the benchmark.

76
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.950
Beating it is the only reason to

77
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.080
run a strategy instead of just holding.

78
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.330
And in this backtest,

79
00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.740
BTC 1D beats it on all three.

80
00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:34.390
Trades.

81
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.720
Closed trades in the window.

82
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.520
12.

83
00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:38.720
And win rate.

84
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.010
The share of trades that made money.

85
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:41.790
67%.

86
00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.760
On its own, it says little.

87
00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.440
A strategy can win most trades and still

88
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.140
lose if the few losses are large.

89
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.500
So read it next to MAR and max drawdown.

90
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.980
Every column has an info button.

91
00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.400
Hover it and the definition appears.

92
00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.570
You can also sort by any column.

93
00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:02.690
Tap max drawdown and the table sorts by it.

94
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.500
Tap again and it flips.

95
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.030
Tap the hash to return to the ranking.

96
00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.810
On the right, the live block.

97
00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.830
These three columns do not depend on the window.

98
00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.010
Last run.

99
00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.550
When this product signal was last calculated.

100
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:16.550
Last change.

101
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.340
The last completed action.

102
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.360
What it exited with that trades

103
00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.170
result and what it entered.

104
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.690
And position today.

105
00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.920
What the strategy holds right now.

106
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.510
Asset, weight, and side or cash.

107
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.810
When a signal is being refreshed or is overdue,

108
00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.040
a pill says so.

109
00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.800
The access column shows a check

110
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.950
when your plan includes the product.

111
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.430
Tap the product name and its

112
00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.090
live card opens right here,

113
00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.290
inside the table.

114
00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.830
It is the same card as in the

115
00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.730
Catalog and the Catalog video explains it.

116
00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.310
The table updates every day after the close.

117
00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:51.090
Everything here is a simulated backtest,

118
00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.670
not real performance, and not investment advice.

